{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc 'cat __issue_context__.json'","aggregated_output":"{\n  \"body\": \"Hi!  My suggestion is to change the term name to \\\"chronic myeloid leukemia\\\" as it is the preferred and most common name, with \\\"Chronic Myelogenous Leukemia\\\" being an older synonym;   I understand that the full name \\\"Chronic Myelogenous Leukemia, BCR-ABL1 positive\\\" is more precise because CML is defined by the presence of the BCR-ABL1 gene, distinguishing it from rare CML-like disorders, and should be kept as a synonym. \\n\\nChronic myeloid leukemia is the standard term used by the National Cancer Institute, and National Institutes of Health, and major health organizations like the American Cancer Society,\\nPlease see: \\nhttps://www.cancer.gov/types/leukemia/patient/cml-treatment-pdq\\nhttps://medlineplus.gov/genetics/condition/chronic-myeloid-leukemia/#synonyms\\nhttps://www.cancer.org/cancer/types/chronic-myeloid-leukemia/about/what-is-cml.html\\n\\nThank you,  Gioconda Alyea\\n\\n\",\n  \"comments\": [],\n  \"title\": \"chronic myelogenous leukemia, BCR-ABL1 positive\",\n  \"url\": \"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/9892\"\n}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
